  "notes": "JAPANESE FOOD PRESENTATION:\n{盛|も}り{付|つ}け is an important aspect of Japanese cuisine, where visual beauty is valued alongside taste.\n\nPRINCIPLES:\n- {余白|よはく}: leaving white space\n- {高|たか}さを{出|だ}す: creating height\n- {色|いろ}の{バランス|ばらんす}: color balance\n- {奇数|きすう}を{好|この}む: preference for odd numbers\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {盛|も}り{付|つ}けをする: to plate food\n- {盛|も}り{付|つ}けが{美|うつく}しい: beautiful presentation\n- {盛|も}り{付|つ}け{方|かた}: way of plating\n\nRELATED TERMS:\n- {盛|も}る: to heap, serve food\n- プレゼンテーション: presentation (loanword)",
